---
description: Repository guidance for the scientific Persian translation skill.
alwaysApply: true
---

Guidance for Cursor when working **on** this repository. The skill's own
instructions are in `scientific-fa-translation-skill/SKILL.md`; do not
restate them here, so there is one place to change them. `CLAUDE.md` and
`AGENTS.md` carry the same guidance for Claude Code and Codex.

The skill payload is the `scientific-fa-translation-skill/` directory.
Install it by copying that directory — not the repo root — into
`~/.cursor/skills/`, exactly one level deep. The frontmatter `name` must
keep matching the directory name.

Repo rules: keep `SKILL.md` short and tool-neutral; the terminology policy
lives only in `references/terminology.md`; a machine-checkable rule goes in
`scripts/check-fa.py` with a fixture in `tests/fixtures/`, then
`bash tests/run.sh`. Paths in prose use `$HOME/...`.

If a user asks *in this workspace* to translate a scientific document into
Persian, read `scientific-fa-translation-skill/SKILL.md` and follow it.
Agent chat is not the RTL surface: write a PDF to `$HOME/Documents/books`
and keep chat to a short pointer.
